\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces {\bf  Stages of T1D}  The progression of T1D follows three recognized stages. \textbf  {Stage 1} marks the onset of Islet Autoimmunity (IA), with the presence of two or more diabetes-related autoantibodies but normal blood glucose levels. \textbf  {Stage 2} is characterized by worsening $\beta $-cell function and emerging dysglycemia, despite the absence of symptoms. \textbf  {Stage 3} is the clinical onset of T1D, marked by symptomatic hyperglycemia requiring insulin therapy \cite  {Type1Diabetes,onengut-gumuscuGeneticVariantsComplement2024}.}}{1}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:stages_t1d}{{1}{1}{{\bf Stages of T1D}\\ The progression of T1D follows three recognized stages. \textbf {Stage 1} marks the onset of Islet Autoimmunity (IA), with the presence of two or more diabetes-related autoantibodies but normal blood glucose levels. \textbf {Stage 2} is characterized by worsening $\beta $-cell function and emerging dysglycemia, despite the absence of symptoms. \textbf {Stage 3} is the clinical onset of T1D, marked by symptomatic hyperglycemia requiring insulin therapy \cite {Type1Diabetes,onengut-gumuscuGeneticVariantsComplement2024}}{figure.caption.6}{}}
