\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces {\bf  Shannon's $3^{\text  {rd}}$ Property of $H$}   This is a decomposition of a choice from three possibilities. The {\bf  left tree} has \textit  {one choice} with probabilities $p_{l1}=\frac  {1}{2}, p_{l2}=\frac  {1}{3}, p_{l3}=\frac  {1}{6}$ and the {\bf  right tree} has \textit  {two choices} with the first having equal probability $p_{r1}=p_{r2}=\frac  {1}{2}$ and the second having probabilities $p_{r21}=\frac  {2}{3},p_{r22}=\frac  {1}{3}$\cite  {shannonMathematicalTheoryCommunication}.}}{8}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
