\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces {\bf  Diffusion Intuition}  The graph on the {\bf  left} depicts nodes 1 and 7 as "hot", while the remaining nodes are "cold". After diffusion (graph on the {\bf  right}), node 1 has "cooled" as it transfers heat to its direct neighbors—and to a lesser extent, its indirect neighbors—demonstrating the spread of information. In contrast, node 7 remains "hot" due to its lack of connections.}}{14}{figure.caption.15}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:diffusion}{{9}{14}{{\bf Diffusion Intuition}\\ The graph on the {\bf left} depicts nodes 1 and 7 as "hot", while the remaining nodes are "cold". After diffusion (graph on the {\bf right}), node 1 has "cooled" as it transfers heat to its direct neighbors—and to a lesser extent, its indirect neighbors—demonstrating the spread of information. In contrast, node 7 remains "hot" due to its lack of connections}{figure.caption.15}{}}
